      "message": "Done for adding CONFIG_ROM_BASE description in config.h.\n\nFor board zinger and hadoken both have a cortex-m0, so they won\u0027t get affected by cortex-m linker script change.\n\nFor board stm32l476g-eval, \"#undef CONFIG_FLASH_PHSYICAL\" is guarded by __ASSEMBLER__, and this is also not affected by the linker script change (linker script only runs preprocessor).\n\nBesides of undefining CONFIG_FLASH_PHYSICAL, should we add new config CONFIG_ROM for the boards which really need a ROM instead?\n\nFor instance, a board without flash, and it doesn\u0027t need a ROM, it can do\n\n\n#undef CONFIG_FLASH_PHYSICAL\n\n\na board without flash, and it needs a ROM, it can do\n\n\n#undef CONFIG_FLASH_PHYSICAL\n#define CONFIG_ROM\n\n\nNot sure if we should do this or not, since the linker script is  complicated enough...",
